# Amendment — corpus-inlining SessionStart hook
#
# 2026-04-28. Per the locked plan-doc
# `docs/rebuild/plans/corpus-inlining-session-start-hook.md`,
# locked research artefact
# `docs/rebuild/plans/research/corpus-inlining-session-start-hook-research.md`,
# and builder plan
# `docs/rebuild/plans/corpus-inlining-session-start-hook.builder-plan.md`.
#
# This amendment closes the corpus-load failure class flagged in
# FIDRAFT (entry "SessionStart corpus_gate should inline corpus
# content into additionalContext, not just verify presence",
# captured 2026-04-28). Per ODD §5.1.1 this is *elimination* of
# the failure class, not relocation: the always-load corpus enters
# `additionalContext` at session-start; "always read corpus at
# session-start" stops being an advisory rule in MEMORY.md prose
# and becomes a substrate property — the model has the bytes in
# context the moment the session opens.
#
# The hook composes on existing A1 substrate primitives only. No
# new substrate; one more consumer of an existing one. Per Lens 1
# this is a recursive instance of the structural-enforcement
# programme finding: Claude Code's hook surface IS the structural-
# enforcement surface. Per Lens 2 the persona's translation
# burden drops (no rule to remember; the corpus is in context
# already) and the harness gains a new primitive (`corpus is in
# context` is a session-level harness property).
#
# Surface added (hands-off-lifecycle, sealed):
#
#   - `framework/hands-off-lifecycle/hooks/corpus_inline_session_start.py`
#     (new) — pure-stdlib SessionStart inner-hook script.
#     Reads SessionStart JSON envelope from stdin; resolves
#     workspace_root + session_id; reads workspace_mode via A1's
#     `corpus_load_sentinel.workspace_mode`; NORMAL USE → exit 0
#     empty stdout (AC.CI.3); DEV MODE → reads the static lean
#     always-load tier ({CLAUDE.md, VALUE_PROPOSITION.md,
#     STATE.md}) via duplicated `_resolve_corpus_path` helper
#     (workspace-root → framework subdir fall-through per #67
#     contract); emits per-file delimited content blocks to stdout
#     under a `=== pos-v2 always-loaded corpus (DEV MODE) ===`
#     banner; emits an `=== pos-v2 on-demand corpus ===` pointer
#     block listing on-demand workspace-relative paths
#     ({odd-methodology.md, odd-in-pos.md, FUTURE_IDEAS.md});
#     per-file 50_000-char ceiling with truncation marker
#     (AC.CI.6); updates A1's sentinel `corpus_paths_loaded` with
#     the inlined paths via the extended `write_corpus_load_sentinel`
#     surface (AC.CI.4); fail-soft on every error path (exit 0,
#     never raises into the SessionStart fan-out, AC.CI.7); 5s
#     SessionStart inner-hook budget (matches A1 / loam-mode /
#     persona precedent).
#   - `framework/hands-off-lifecycle/hooks/corpus_load_sentinel.py`
#     EXTENDED in-place. `write_corpus_load_sentinel` gains an
#     additional keyword-only parameter `corpus_paths_loaded:
#     list[str] | tuple[str, ...] | None = None`. Backwards-compat
#     by default-None — every existing call site (A1's
#     corpus_load_session_start.py CLI) still works without
#     change. When provided, the loaded list is serialised into
#     the sentinel JSON's `corpus_paths_loaded` field, and the
#     `state` field is recomputed from
#     `corpus_paths_loaded` ⊆ `corpus_paths_required` membership
#     (loaded / partial / missing). When None, the legacy
#     path-existence-derived `state` semantics are preserved.
#   - `framework/hands-off-lifecycle/hooks/first_run_settings.py`
#     — `_POS_V2_COMMAND_MARKERS` extended with
#     `corpus_inline_session_start.py` so re-merge over a stanza
#     we wrote does not back up the corpus-inline inner hook as
#     user-authored.
#   - `framework/hands-off-lifecycle/hooks/first_run_helper.py`
#     — adds `_corpus_inline_inner_hooks(pos_v2_root)` builder
#     mirroring `_corpus_load_inner_hooks` shape (5s timeout).
#     `_extra_session_start_hooks` is REORDERED: prior order
#     (persona → loam-mode → corpus-load) → new order (corpus-load
#     → corpus-inline → persona → loam-mode). The relative
#     ordering A1 → corpus-inline → persona is locked per plan
#     §6 D-build.4 / D-CI.6.(a) so the persona's dossier reads
#     A1's sentinel post-inline (a future micro-amendment can
#     grow a `corpus_inlined: true` marker without re-ordering).
#     AC46.5 stanza-builder tests do NOT pin the order out of
#     `_extra_session_start_hooks` (they pass extras directly to
#     the builder); the re-ordering is internal composition.
#   - `framework/hands-off-lifecycle/tests/test_AC_CI_*.py` (8
#     files, AC.CI.1..AC.CI.7 + AC.CI.S) — outcome-shaped per the
#     locked plan-doc §4. Per ODD §8.2.14 byte-content
#     verification, the AC.CI.4 test reads the on-disk sentinel
#     JSON and asserts schema; the AC.CI.1 + AC.CI.2 + AC.CI.6
#     tests grep the hook's stdout for the documented markers.
#
# Behaviour:
#
#   - DEV MODE (workspace_mode == "dev-mode"): hook fires; reads
#     the always-load tier from disk; emits content blocks +
#     pointer block to stdout (Claude Code captures stdout as
#     `additionalContext` per the established loam-mode + persona
#     emitter convention); updates A1's per-(workspace, session)
#     sentinel `corpus_paths_loaded` field with the actually-
#     inlined paths; sentinel `state` reflects the loaded subset.
#   - NORMAL USE (workspace_mode != "dev-mode"): hook fires;
#     observes mode bit; exits 0 with empty stdout; no sentinel
#     update. Persona's existing #46 dossier remains the NORMAL
#     USE shape unchanged.
#   - Path resolution: workspace-root probe first; fall-through
#     to `<workspace>/framework/<rel>` matches #67's reader
#     contract bit-for-bit. Workspace-root copy wins; framework-
#     only-clone shape is supported transparently.
#   - Per-file ceiling: 50_000 chars per file; truncation marker
#     `[truncated at 50000 chars; full file at <path>]` emitted
#     when the ceiling is hit. Other files in the same fire are
#     unaffected.
#   - Fail-soft: every error path returns exit 0. Missing always-
#     load files emit a `[missing]` marker; missing on-demand
#     files are silently omitted from the pointer block. Sentinel
#     write failure does NOT block stdout emission — the hook's
#     primary job is content emission, sentinel update is the
#     bookkeeping side-effect.
#
# Token budget verification (build-time):
#
#   - Always-load tier measured size (canonical pos-v2 HEAD,
#     2026-04-28): CLAUDE.md = 4,778 chars; VALUE_PROPOSITION.md
#     = 11,479 chars; STATE.md = 10,948 chars. Total = 27,205
#     chars ≈ 6,800 tokens (4:1 ratio). Within plan §6 D-CI.1
#     expected ~6.8k. Headroom against the persona's 10k-char
#     `ADDITIONAL_CONTEXT_CAP` is irrelevant — the new hook's
#     stdout is a separate stanza, not bound by the persona's
#     per-stanza cap (research §3.2). Cumulative session-start
#     emission well under any reasonable ceiling.
#
# Mode-aware partition (programme D4 lock + plan §6 D-build.8):
# this hook is DEV-MODE-only per D-CI.8. NORMAL USE workspaces
# have no shared corpus to read (no docs/odd-methodology.md, no
# docs/rebuild/STATE.md); inlining what doesn't exist degrades
# to no-op anyway. Consistency with A1 D4 (ODD-discipline gates
# DEV-MODE-only).
#
# AC surface (AC.CI.1 – AC.CI.7 + AC.CI.S) — outcome-shaped per
# the locked plan-doc §4. Behaviour count = 8; ACs declared = 8.
# Forward + reverse match.
#
# ODD §2.5 reverse-direction audit clean: every code path,
# branch, dependency, and test in the diff traces back to a
# named AC. No silent exception branches; no defensive `if`
# for cases the ACs do not name; no method-in-AC drift. Builder
